bel":"Chemical"},{"text":"S-312-l","id":"2","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"flunarizine","id":"3","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"pentylenetetrazole","id":"4","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"bemegride","id":"5","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"N-methyl-D-aspartate","id":"6","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"picrotoxin","id":"7","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"electroshock","id":"8","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"audiogenic tonic convulsions","id":"1","label":"Disease"}],"gold_relations":"picrotoxin | CID | convulsions\npentylenetetrazole | CID | convulsions\nbemegride | CID | convulsions","labels":"Chemical,Disease","metrics":{"precision":0.0,"recall":0.0,"f1":0.0,"tp":0,"fp":0,"fn":3,"rel_precision":0.0,"rel_recall":0.0,"rel_f1":0.0,"rel_tp":0,"rel_fp":0,"rel_fn":3},"pairs":[{"head":"dihydrothienopyridine calcium antagonist","tail":"audiogenic tonic convulsions","head_id":"1","tail_id":"1"},{"head":"S-312-l","tail":"audiogenic tonic convulsions","head_id":"2","tail_id":"1"},{"head":"flunarizine","tail":"audiogenic tonic convulsions","head_id":"3","tail_id":"1"},{"head":"pentylenetetrazole","tail":"audiogenic tonic convulsions","head_id":"4","tail_id":"1"},{"head":"bemegride","tail":"audiogenic tonic convulsions","head_id":"5","tail_id":"1"},{"head":"N-methyl-D-aspartate","tail":"audiogenic tonic convulsions","head_id":"6","tail_id":"1"},{"head":"picrotoxin","tail":"audiogenic tonic convulsions","head_id":"7","tail_id":"1"},{"head":"electroshock","tail":"audiogenic tonic convulsions","head_id":"8","tail_id":"1"}],"text":"Pharmacological studies on a new dihydrothienopyridine calcium antagonist, S-312-d. 5th communication: anticonvulsant effects in mice. S-312, S-312-d, but not S-312-l, L-type calcium channel antagonists, showed anticonvulsant effects on the audiogenic tonic convulsions in DBA/2 mice; and their ED50 values were 18.4 (12.8-27.1) mg/kg, p.o. and 15.0 (10.2-23.7) mg/kg, p.o., respectively, while that of flunarizine was 34.0 (26.0-44.8) mg/kg, p.o. Although moderate anticonvulsant effects of S-312-d in higher doses were observed against the clonic convulsions induced by pentylenetetrazole (85 mg/kg, s.c.) or bemegride (40 mg/kg, s.c.), no effects were observed in convulsions induced by N-methyl-D-aspartate, picrotoxin, or electroshock in Slc:ddY mice. S-312-d may be useful in the therapy of certain types of human epilepsy."}